# Suderra CA Certificate
# Replace this file with the actual Suderra root CA PEM certificate before building production firmware.
# The provisioning client uses this certificate to pin TLS connections to the cloud API,
# preventing MITM attacks via compromised system CAs (IEC 62443 FR4).
#
# To generate for development/testing:
#   openssl req -x509 -newkey rsa:4096 -keyout suderra-ca-key.pem -out suderra-ca.pem \
#           -days 3650 -nodes -subj "/CN=Suderra CA"
#
# IMPORTANT: This placeholder will cause the build to fail at TLS handshake.
# You MUST replace it with a valid CA PEM before deploying to production.
-----BEGIN CERTIFICATE-----
PLACEHOLDER - REPLACE WITH ACTUAL SUDERRA CA CERTIFICATE
-----END CERTIFICATE-----
